# Tolerance classes used by the Physics2D test suite.
#
# Comparisons against Box2D golden fixtures need looser tolerances than
# Physics2D-internal checks because upstream C stores results in 32-bit floats
# while Physics2D computes in Double. Fixture values are printed with nine
# significant digits, which alone introduces up to roughly 5e-8 relative error.
# Accumulated quantities diverge further because upstream arithmetic rounds at
# every float32 step. Each tolerance records its rationale; do not weaken a
# tolerance without recording why.
Module Tolerances
# Pure arithmetic compared against nine-digit C output.
Const MATHS_ABS As Double = 0.000000000001
Const MATHS_REL As Double = 0.000001

# Hull, distance, and cast results computed from float32 intermediates.
Const GEOMETRY_ABS As Double = 0.00000001
Const GEOMETRY_REL As Double = 0.00001

# Manifold points, normals, and separations. Upstream clips with float32
# arithmetic and snaps small values, so absolute error dominates.
Const MANIFOLD_ABS As Double = 0.00005
Const MANIFOLD_REL As Double = 0.0001

# Mass properties integrate over polygon areas.
Const MASS_ABS As Double = 0.0001
Const MASS_REL As Double = 0.0001

# Body transforms after a full simulation scene. Upstream float32 rounding
# compounds every substep, so scene comparisons are the loosest class.
Const SCENE_ABS As Double = 0.002
Const SCENE_REL As Double = 0.002

# Distance-joint constraint forces, torques, and motor forces after a full
# simulation scene. The reported force is the applied solver impulse divided
# by the substep size, so the float32 impulse error is amplified by 1/h =
# 240. Impulses match to well under 1e-5 in the golden scenes, giving a
# worst-case force error around 2.4e-3 N; 0.01 N absolute keeps a safety
# factor of about four while staying far below the 2.5 N body weight scale
# of the fixtures. Relative tolerance covers the saturated 2000 N motor
# force.
Const JOINT_FORCE_ABS As Double = 0.01
Const JOINT_FORCE_REL As Double = 0.001

# Physics2D-internal checks that never compare against C output.
Const INTERNAL_ABS As Double = 0.000000000001
Const INTERNAL_REL As Double = 0.000000000001

# Upstream deterministic trigonometric approximations compared against the
# platform library. Physics2D ports b2Atan2 (float-precision minimax
# coefficients; measured maximum deviation about 2.8e-5 radians) and
# b2ComputeCosSin (Bhaskara-style approximation; measured maximum deviation
# about 1.7e-3). The tolerances sit above those measured bounds.
Const ATAN2_ABS As Double = 0.00005
Const TRIG_ABS As Double = 0.0025

# Upstream test_math.c recovers an angle with b2Atan2 over the approximate
# sin/cos pair and compares against the unwound angle using 4e-4. In Double
# the approximate components carry up to about 1.7e-3 of angular error
# themselves, which the atan recovery propagates; the measured maximum over
# the upstream sweep is about 1.7e-3 radians, so this tolerance sits above
# that bound instead of the upstream constant.
Const TRIG_RECOVERY_ABS As Double = 0.0025

# The ComputeCosSin pair is normalised to the unit circle in Double, so its
# length deviates by rounding only.
Const TRIG_NORM_ABS As Double = 0.000000000001

# Deterministic checksums must match exactly.
Const EXACT As Double = 0.0
End Module
